# The format of this file is identical to `.dockerignore`.
# It is used to reduce the size of deployed images to make the process of publishing faster.
#
# This list is load-bearing. A publish failed while uploading the repl layer with
# `io: read/write on closed pipe` on a file inside target/debug/deps — the
# workspace is roughly 20 GB and the Rust build cache alone is 15 GB of it.
# Everything excluded below is either rebuilt by scripts/replit-build.sh or was
# never needed to serve the app.

# ── Build caches: rebuilt during the publish build ──
# The release binary is copied to deploy-bin/, which is deliberately NOT ignored;
# nothing that must reach the image may be left inside target/.
target
node_modules
frontend/node_modules
.cache
.upm

# ── History and agent scratch space ──
.git
.local
.agents
.config

# ── Archives, captures and working material, not part of the running app ──
**/*.zip
**/*.tar.gz
attached_assets
downloads
screenshots

# ── Exceptions: shipped on purpose, despite the rules above ──
# Served by GET /api/install/source.tar.gz (crates/yoda-api/src/install.rs).
# Without it the published installer hands out a 404.
!downloads/yoda-workspace-snapshot.tar.gz
